\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lead kindly Light, amid the encircling gloom
\par Lead Thou me on!
\par The night is dark and I am far from home;
\par Lead Thou me on!
\par Keep Thou my feet; I do not ask to see
\par The distant scene: one step enough for me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I was not ever thus, nor prayed that Thou
\par Shouldst lead me on.
\par I loved to choose and see my path, but now
\par Lead Thou me on!
\par I loved the garish day, and, spite of fears,
\par Pride ruled my will: remember not past years.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. So long the power hath blest me, sure it still
\par Will lead me on
\par O'er moor and fen, o'er crag and torrent, till
\par The night is gone;
\par And with the morn those angel faces smile
\par Which I have loved long since, and lost awhile.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

